From: Pi <pi@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: do not wait for userspace on the optional fw api 2 image

ath12k_fw_map() probes for the "fw api 2" image (firmware-2.bin) and falls
back to the split amss/m3 images (q6_fw0.mdt + q6_fw1.mdt) when it is not
available.  The probe used request_firmware_nowarn(), which still goes
through the userspace fallback path: when the file is absent the firmware
loader waits the full FW_LOAD_TIMEOUT_MS (60 s) for a userspace helper to
supply it before returning -ETIMEDOUT.

The IPQ5332 firmware releases used by the JDCloud RE-CS-600/BE6500 do not
ship firmware-2.bin at all (only q6_fw0.* / q6_fw1.*), so every boot was
stalled for a minute inside ath12k_wifi7_ahb_probe() before the Q6 remote
processor was powered up:

  [    8.747] ath12k_wifi7_ahb c000000.wifi: Wi-Fi 7 Hardware name: ipq5332 hw1.0
  [   69.596] ath12k_wifi7_ahb c000000.wifi: failed to load firmware-2.bin: -110
  [   69.596] ath12k_wifi7_ahb c000000.wifi: using fw api 1
  [   69.601] remoteproc remoteproc0: powering up q6wcss

Use request_firmware_direct() for this optional probe so the missing file is
reported immediately (-ENOENT instead of -ETIMEDOUT) and the fallback to
fw api 1 happens right away:

  [    8.934] ath12k_wifi7_ahb c000000.wifi: Wi-Fi 7 Hardware name: ipq5332 hw1.0
  [    8.958] ath12k_wifi7_ahb c000000.wifi: failed to load firmware-2.bin: -2
  [    8.966] remoteproc remoteproc0: powering up q6wcss
  [    9.157] remoteproc remoteproc0: remote processor q6wcss is now up

Because the change is limited to this single optional request, the global
userspace fallback path (needed by other drivers) stays enabled.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/fw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/fw.c
@@ -7,6 +7,33 @@
 
 #include "debug.h"
 
+/*
+ * The fw api 2 image is optional: when it is missing the driver falls back to
+ * the split amss/m3 images.  Use request_firmware_direct() so a missing file
+ * fails immediately instead of blocking the probe for the full 60 second
+ * userspace fallback timeout (FW_LOAD_TIMEOUT_MS).  On IPQ5332 the fw api 2
+ * image is not shipped at all, so the blocking behaviour added a minute to
+ * every boot.
+ */
+static const struct firmware *ath12k_fw_request_optional(struct ath12k_base *ab,
+							 const char *name)
+{
+	const struct firmware *fw;
+	char path[100];
+	int ret;
+
+	ath12k_core_create_firmware_path(ab, name, path, sizeof(path));
+
+	ret = request_firmware_direct(&fw, path, ab->dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ERR_PTR(ret);
+
+	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_BOOT, "boot firmware request %s size %zu\n",
+		   path, fw->size);
+
+	return fw;
+}
+
 static int ath12k_fw_request_firmware_api_n(struct ath12k_base *ab,
 					    const char *name)
 {
@@ -16,7 +43,7 @@
 	const u8 *data;
 	__le32 *timestamp;
 
-	ab->fw.fw = ath12k_core_firmware_request(ab, name);
+	ab->fw.fw = ath12k_fw_request_optional(ab, name);
 	if (IS_ERR(ab->fw.fw)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(ab->fw.fw);
 		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_BOOT, "failed to load %s: %d\n", name, ret);
